{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:0.2", "PA_thag_2.43:0.3"], "en": "Pañcamavagga The Elder’s Verses, Book Two, Chapter Five, Verse 43.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:0.4"], "en": "The Verses of the Elder Brahmāli:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:1.1"], "en": "“Whose faculties have reached tranquility,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:1.2"], "en": "like horses well-tamed by a charioteer?”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:1.3", "PA_thag_2.43:1.4"], "en": "\"Even the gods envy him who has abandoned conceit, who is free from taints, and who is such;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:2.1"], "en": "his faculties have entered into tranquility. Thus spoke the Sage.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:2.2"], "en": "“Just as horses well-tamed by a charioteer,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:2.3", "PA_thag_2.43:2.4"], "en": "even the gods envy me, who am free from conceit and free from taints, such as I am.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_2.43:2.5"], "en": "… the Elder Brahmāli …", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"}
